      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Length Lives In The Type",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`[5]int` and `[6]int` are different types — no assignment",
            "Arrays are values: assigning or passing copies every element",
            "`len()` of an array is a compile-time constant, foldable",
            "`[3]int{1,2,3}` IS the data; `[...]int{1,2,3}` lets the compiler count"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var a [5]int",
            "var b [6]int",
            "a = b // compile error: type mismatch",
            "c := a // full copy of 5 ints"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Slice Header",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "memory-cells",
          "spec": {
            "label": "slice header = 24 bytes",
            "cells": [
              "ptr *T",
              "len int",
              "cap int"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A slice is not an array — it is a 3-word struct",
            "Copying a slice copies 3 words, never the elements",
            "`ptr` points into a backing array living elsewhere",
            "Slice literal `[]int{1,2,3}` allocates an array of 3, points at it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "len Is The Gate, cap Is The Room"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "field",
            "meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`len`",
              "indexable count"
            ],
            [
              "`cap`",
              "`ptr` to array end"
            ],
            [
              "`len<cap`",
              "spare room"
            ],
            [
              "index `>= len`",
              "panic"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Larger cap does not save you",
          "text": "`s := make([]int,3,8); s[5]` still panics: `runtime error: index out of range [5] with length 3`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "nil Slice vs Empty Slice",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var s []int   // nil: ptr=nil len=0 cap=0",
            "t := []int{}  // non-nil, len 0",
            "// both len 0, but s==nil is true"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "value",
            "`== nil`",
            "JSON"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`var s []int`",
              "true",
              "`null`"
            ],
            [
              "`[]int{}`",
              "false",
              "`[]`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The nil slice is safe to `append`, `range` and `len()`",
            "Slices are not comparable: `s1 == s2` is a compile error",
            "Only `s == nil` is allowed by the spec"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Which one to reach for",
