          "text": "The Three-Index Form"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "t := s[1:3:3] // cap = max-low = 2",
            "// cap == len, so append must copy",
            "u := s[i:j:j] // defensive handoff"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "`s[low:high:max]`",
          "text": "Sets `cap = max-low`, clamping how far a later append can reach into your array."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pinned Memory",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The array stays alive while ANY slice points at it",
            "A 3-byte slice of a 10 MB read pins all 10 MB",
            "Cure: copy out what you actually need"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "out := make([]byte, len(part))",
            "copy(out, part)   // part is free now",
