      "page_title": "append and Growth Mechanics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Known `n` removes every intermediate copy and its garbage",
            "`make([]T,n)` then append is the classic off-by-n bug",
            "`slices.Grow(s,n)` reserves room without touching `len`",
            "`slices.Clip(s)` returns `s[:len(s):len(s)]`, cap cut to len"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Bulk Appends"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "s = append(s, other...)  // whole slice",
            "b = append(b, \"str\"...)  // string into []byte"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "op",
            "cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "index / append",
              "O(1), O(1) amortized"
            ],
            [
              "prepend",
              "O(n)"
            ],
            [
              "delete ordered / swap",
              "O(n) / O(1)"
            ],
            [
              "copy / search",
              "O(n) / O(n)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Core Hazard",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Whether append mutates a shared array or forks a private copy depends on spare capacity. Capacity is a runtime property nobody can see at the call site."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "a := []int{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}",
            "b := a[:2]          // len 2, cap 5",
            "b = append(b, 99)   // spare cap!",
            "// a is now {1,2,99,4,5}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Worst kind of nondeterminism",
          "text": "The same code is correct or broken depending on capacity the caller never sees and never wrote."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Header Is A Copy",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A function taking `[]T` CAN mutate the caller's elements",
            "Passing a slice protects the header, not the data",
            "It CANNOT change the caller's `len` — return the result"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
